    "review_conclusions": [
      "All 78 fixed-scope files were read and their SHA-256 values exactly match the scope. This includes all ten formal blessing pages, the author-approved config/draft and source/UI/image receipts, the generated candidate snapshot, map, shared catalogue, and reverse weapon pages.",
      "The four actual variants and seven bindings in BLESSING_WEAPON_MAP match the scope: autopistol_p1 (1), bolter_p1 (2), dual_autopistols_p1 (1), and ogryn_heavystubber_p2 (3). All four associated reverse weapon pages link the exact variant IDs; actual UI names and marks in the formal page match the UI receipt. Available tiers remain null.",
      "The four own I–IV tables show 4.25%, 4.5%, 4.75%, and 5% generic power per effective layer, with five effective layers and a shared 2.5-second refresh window. The own-tier and wrapper receipts support each weapon-specific tier override and clone/child wiring; the common base trigger conditions are applied only where the bound wrapper uses them.",
      "Player text accurately distinguishes the source-item and currently-wielded gates, actual stagger-result gate, per-event layer gain, expiry/cache timing, and the Adamant melee-weakspot exception. It states that a triggering hit resolves before the newly added layer can affect later attacks.",
      "The actual action coverage is consistent with the bound templates: ordinary hip/aim hitscan, Bolter conditional stop/kill explosion, Bolter and Dual Autopistols special melee sweeps, flashlight-toggle specials for Autopistol and Heavy Stubber, and pure-push event distinction. The Bolter explosion path retains the source item, uses explosion attack type, and still requires that target to stagger and the source weapon to be held; the generic power modifier is read from the attacker cache for target attacks.",
      "The controlled example uses the actual Autopistol P1 M1 path and explicitly treats P_curve=100 as a normalized intermediate power input, not fixed damage. Formula and tier totals are described as power-stage changes rather than guaranteed final health-damage percentages.",
      "The exact English/Traditional Chinese localization keys and hashes, formatter/static I–IV reconstruction, rule classifications, icon identity, and image receipt are consistent. The formal change from the accepted source review is limited to removing an unproved UI-placeholder phrase and adding the live-player sender source reference; gameplay values and mechanics remain unchanged.",
      "Focused scope review and independent map/reverse-link assertions passed; no unresolved issue found."
    ],
